<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keladi Nayakas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1499–<a href="/years/1763">1763</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Nayakas of Ikkeri, Ikkeri Nayakas, Nayakas of Keladi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keladi">Keladi</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayakas</a>, also called the Nayakas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikkeri">Ikkeri</a>, were a dynasty that ruled the coast and western hills of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> from about 1499 to 1763, first as governors under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and then independently. Their capitals were successively Keladi, Ikkeri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bednur">Bidanur</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> conquered their kingdom in 1763.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/keladi-nayakas.jpg" alt="Keladi Nayakas" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: H. SHASHIDHAR of the Indian Administrative Service and N. SREENIVASA MURTHY Geographer of the DCD, Karnataka. DIRECTO... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greatest_Extent_Of_Keladi_Kingdom_during_the_reign_of_Shivappa_Nayaka.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
